/* The canonical Mahabalipuram monument list — shared by the destination page
 * (js/place.js, which renders the cards and the flythrough) and the on-site
 * visitor guide (js/guide-map.js).
 *
 * ---- COORDINATES ----
 * `osm` is the OpenStreetMap element this monument corresponds to. It is the
 * coordinate reference, and it is deliberately the ONLY coordinate link here:
 * the numbers live in data/mahabalipuram-osm.json (regenerated by
 * `node scripts/fetch-site-data.js`), so the mapping stays human-checked while
 * the coordinates stay current with OSM.
 *
 * An entry whose `osm` id is not in that dump gets coordFor() === null and its
 * pin silently disappears — so `node scripts/fetch-site-data.js --offline` is
 * the gate that must pass before shipping a new entry.
 *
 * Why OSM and not Wikidata: Wikidata's coordinates for this site are bad.
 * Varaha Cave (Q7915405) is ~18 km out — a longitude typo — and Descent of the
 * Ganges, Mahishasuramardini and Olakkanneshwara all share one rounded
 * placeholder ~200 m from where they actually are.
 *
 * ---- PROSE ----
 * Descriptions are written from Wikipedia's "Group of Monuments at
 * Mahabalipuram" (NOT the "Mamallapuram" article, which is town history and
 * transport). That text is CC BY-SA: PARAPHRASE IT, never paste it. Anything
 * quoted verbatim goes in “…” with the source, exactly as
 * content/mahabalipuram-heights.js already does. Every entry carries
 * `sources[]` with a section-anchored URL and an `accessed` date.
 *
 * ---- FIELDS ----
 *   id        slug. NEVER rename — #stop= links in the wild use these.
 *   title     shown on the pin and the card. Must disambiguate: Dharmaraja
 *             Ratha and Dharmaraja Mandapa are different monuments 700 m apart.
 *   when      free text period
 *   wiki      Wikipedia article title for the photo lookup, or null
 *   photo     AUTHORED, verified against the API. false => the guide makes no
 *             request and reserves no image box. This is what makes the page
 *             honest offline rather than showing an empty frame.
 *   text      ONE string — the card blurb. js/place.js renders this. Do not
 *             turn it into an array; that file has no guard for it.
 *   detail    extra paragraphs, guide-only. place.js ignores it.
 *   tags      REQUIRED on every entry. js/place.js:33 does m.tags.map() with
 *             no guard, so one entry without it throws and blanks the whole
 *             monuments grid AND the flythrough.
 *   form      what kind of thing it is, for the plan's symbol on the site
 *             plan (js/site-plan.js): cave (excavated into the rock),
 *             monolith (cut free from a boulder), structural (built of
 *             blocks), relief (a carved face), boulder, or group. It
 *             classifies what the cited Wikipedia section says; it is not a
 *             measurement, and the plan says so. Missing => a plain dot.
 *   roof      OPTIONAL, only where the repo already documents it (each carries
 *             a `// source:` comment): pyramidal | barrel | hut | apsidal |
 *             boulder. Picks the plan's picture for a monolith.
 *   picture   OPTIONAL override of the plan's picture where `form` cannot
 *             say (the Shore Temple compound, the unfinished gopuram).
 *   inside    OPTIONAL. "What you will see here" on the guide's card: 3-6
 *             parts, each { n, name, line, more?, stop?, photo? } in plain
 *             words (a line is
 *             about twelve words; `more` two or three sentences, shown when the
 *             part is tapped; `photo` { src, page, author, licence, licenceUrl },
 *             used only when it was looked at and clearly shows that part).
 *             EVERY part must be in this entry's cited
 *             source, in `inside.source`, or in a research note named in the
 *             comment above it. The sketch that goes with it is in
 *             js/monument-diagrams.js, keyed by this entry's id; a part with
 *             no stated position is listed there under `also`, not placed.
 *   feature   in the destination page's flythrough. Kept to the original 8 —
 *             `.fly` height is calc(100vh + steps * 60vh), so putting all 23
 *             in would take that page from ~6 screens of scroll to ~15.
 *   partOf    groups children under a parent (the five rathas)
 *   rank      declutter priority, lower wins
 *   zoomFrom  don't show the pin below this zoom (declutter)
 *
 * ---- DELIBERATELY EXCLUDED ----
 *   node/4121381964, node/5517879855, node/5518300719 — museums, not monuments
 *   node/13078006569 Retro Surf Club, node/7246575985 South Entrance
 *   node/5511537906 "Arunjas Penance Model" — a replica, not the relief
 *   way/390473765 Shore Temple Complex, way/103163461 Group of Monuments —
 *     enclosure/site boundaries, already drawn as the park outline
 *   way/443083327 — unnamed ruin 18 m from Ramanuja Mandapam; unidentifiable,
 *     so excluded rather than guessed at
 *   node/5096042202 "Vālmīkanāthar" — a gazetteer import with no match in the
 *     Wikipedia article
 *   node/5517872769 "Five Celled Rock Cave" — the SAME excavation as Koneri
 *     Mandapam (node/5517874190), double-mapped 7 m away. Wikipedia's §Koneri
 *     says that mandapa "has five cells". One entry shipped, not two.
 *   way/597062775 "Old lighthouse" and way/1552901513 Mahabalipuram Lighthouse
 *     — two different objects ~55 m apart, and the Wikipedia article describes
 *     the 1904 British tower. Neither is Pallava.
 *   relation/8171518 Sthalasayana Perumal — a living temple in the town rather
 *     than part of the monument complex.
 *   node/4433895791 "Devaneri beach" and node/4453036789 "Mumu Surf Club" — a
 *     beach and a surf school, the same class as the Retro Surf Club above.
 *     Both carry only `name:en` and no `name`, which is why they used to appear
 *     nameless in data/mahabalipuram-osm.json; fetch-site-data.js now reads
 *     name:en as a fallback, so they are excluded by WHAT they are, not by
 *     looking mysterious.
 *   node/11672117711 — an unnamed tourism=viewpoint 7 m from way/597062775
 *     "Old lighthouse" and 34 m from Olakkanesvara. The lighthouse-hill
 *     lookout, not a monument of its own.
 *   node/2154131503 — an unnamed historic=archaeological_site at Saluvankuppam,
 *     170 m NE of the Atiranachanda cave. It sits 8 m from ASI N-TN-C112, the
 *     two inscribed rocks, which is the likeliest identification — but the OSM
 *     element carries one tag and no name, so it is excluded as UNIDENTIFIED
 *     rather than guessed at.
 *
 * ---- KNOWN GAP ----
 * Adivaraha Cave Temple has its own Wikipedia section but NO OpenStreetMap
 * record anywhere in either bbox, so there is no coordinate to place it at. It
 * is left out rather than invented. Confirmed absent 2026-09-12 by a Nominatim
 * search on four name variants (0 hits) and an Overpass sweep of every named
 * feature and every place-of-worship on the main hill. It is also the one
 * monument here still in active worship, which is why the ASI does not protect
 * it either.
 *
 * Pulipudar, named in Wikipedia § Other mandapas, likewise has no OSM element
 * and no ASI entry under that name.
 *
 * CORRECTION (2026-09-12): this block used to name Atiranachanda Mandapa here
 * too, and that was WRONG on both counts. It has an OSM record —
 * node/2334799038 — and Saluvankuppam is inside the WIDE bbox (Tiger Cave, at
 * 12.657, is already in this list). The node is tagged only
 * `amenity=place_of_worship; name=Shiva Temple; religion=hindu`, so it matches
 * none of isMonument()'s clauses and was never fetched. That is the Ganesha
 * Ratha failure mode recurring — a real monument invisible to a tag predicate —
 * and the fix is an explicit id in the query, not a broader predicate that
 * would sweep in every modern shrine in town.
 */
const WIKI_GROUP = "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Group_of_Monuments_at_Mahabalipuram";
const SEEN = "2026-09-04";
const src = (section, anchor) => [
  { text: `Wikipedia, “Group of Monuments at Mahabalipuram” § ${section} (CC BY-SA)`, url: `${WIKI_GROUP}#${anchor}`, accessed: SEEN },
];

